<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Africa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Africa is the second-largest continent and the home of many of the empires covered by the site, from the Kushite and Aksumite empires to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti</a> empires. Its trade in gold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a>, salt and later enslaved people connected it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, Islamic, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> and Atlantic worlds. From the fifteenth century onwards European powers such as the Portuguese, British, French and Italian empires established colonies, culminating in the partition of the continent in the late nineteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/africa.jpg" alt="Africa" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martin23230 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Africa_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
